DESCRIPTION:Dan Ghica\nTheoretical Computer Science Seminar\n\nEverything h
 as changed\, and the software engineering landscape will never look the sa
 me. Autonomous coding agents can already produce vast implementations\, di
 smantling the long-held assumption that writing code is the primary constr
 aint of software development. As the marginal cost of code generation beco
 mes negligible\, where does the real bottleneck relocate? Is the new point
  of friction in comprehension\, review\, and verification\, or does the cr
 itical challenge move even higher up the stack\, in specification and vali
 dation? Furthermore\, agent-generated code differs fundamentally from huma
 n-written systems in style\, cognitive idioms\, and architectural failure 
 modes (e.g. slop: plausible…\n\nDetails: https://researchseminars.org/ta
 lk/TheoryCSBham/88/
